      "summary": "Welcome to Module 3 \u2014 the seminar. I\u2019m your instructor, and for this final module we change register: from the archive to the argument. This is Module 3: The CCRU Seminar \u2014 Nick Land and the CCRU (the Warwick 1990s collective: who, where, what; the writings; primary texts in reading order; the archive itself as artifact), hyperstition (fiction as an engine, the hyperstitional circuit, examples and counter-examples \u2014 a CONTESTED theory, labeled as such), the numogram and syzygies (decimal sorcery, working the diagram, reading a technical diagram as a text), meme chaos-magic theory (Spare\u2019s sigilization in the network age, memes as hyperstitional objects, attention as a medium), and Project Cybersyn (Allende\u2019s Chile 1971\u201373, Stafford Beer and the viable system model, the operations room \u2014 what was actually built versus what has been mythologized). Read Land\u2019s 1990s corpus, then argue about what it means \u2014 with tiers.",
